Semantic HTML

Semantic tags describe the purpose of the content.

<header></header>

<nav></nav>

<main></main>

<section></section>

<article></article>

<aside></aside>

<footer></footer>


Why Use Semantic HTML?
Easier to read and maintain.
Better accessibility.
Better SEO.
Frequently asked in interviews.


HTML Interview Questions
Question	Answer

What is HTML?	
HyperText Markup Language used to structure web pages.

Difference between HTML and HTML5?
	HTML5 introduced semantic elements, multimedia support, improved forms, and new APIs.

What is semantic HTML?	HTML elements that describe the meaning of their content, such as header, main, and footer.

Difference between id and class?
	id should be unique on a page; class can be reused on multiple elements.

Difference between div and span?
	div is a block-level container; span is an inline container.

Difference between strong and b?
	strong conveys importance (semantic); b is only a visual bold style.

Why use the alt attribute?	
It improves accessibility and provides fallback text if an image cannot be displayed.

What is the purpose of the viewport meta tag?
	It helps webpages display properly on mobile devices.
